workbook :mcp_server_manifest, type: :design

# MCP server manifest — curated + classified (what we'd run or connect to)

Pulled the OFFICIAL MCP registry (registry.modelcontextprotocol.io): 2900 unique servers. A 97-agent
pass curated + classified them. **2003 niche/single-vendor dropped → 897 kept (170 core, 727 useful).**
Classified along the axes that decide HOW we'd use each one. Re-pull: the registry API; re-classify: the workflow.

## The axes

- **hosting** — *self-host* (a package we compile to wasm + run in Washy) vs *remote* (vendor-hosted, we connect). The decisive one.
- **ui** — *ui* (ships/benefits from an MCP-App panel → the drawer) · *headless* (data/text, background) · *mixed*.
- **runMode** — *one-off* (stateless call) vs *session* (long-lived/stateful → a `worker`).
- **scope** — *team* (shared org capability) · *personal* · *either*.
- **authGated** — needs credentials (→ Nexus.Secrets) vs open.

## The splits (897 kept)

- **hosting:** 281 self-host (run in Washy) · 602 remote (connect)
- **ui:** 76 ui · 359 mixed · 462 headless
- **runMode:** 462 one-off · 435 session
- **scope:** 347 team · 112 personal · 438 either
- **auth:** 595 gated · 302 open
- **domain:** dev 125 · data 125 · infra 105 · ai 101 · web 82 · search 74 · comms 55 · productivity 65 · docs 62 · finance 55 · design 36 · other 12

## ⬛ Start here — self-hostable CORE (66) — compile to wasm, run in Washy

