## Notes

- **self-host = the wasm/Washy candidates.** 66 core are self-hostable packages; the rest are vendor-hosted (connect like an integration).
- **ui-tagged servers feed the drawer** (MCP-App panels). headless ones are background/agent capabilities.
- **session servers = `worker` kind** (long-lived, supervised). one-off = stateless invoke.
- many overlap our 708-integration audit (github/slack/notion/stripe/sentry) — there, the MCP server IS the integration.
